      "text": "### Emily Henry's *People We Meet on Vacation*\n\n#### 1. Publication Background and Reception\n*People We Meet on Vacation* was published in 2021 by Berkley. The novel is a contemporary romance exploring the emotional complexities of friendship and love through the relationship between two best friends, Alex and Poppy. The reception has been largely positive, with critics praising its dual-timeline structure, witty dialogue, and depth in exploring themes like grief and self-discovery. The novel has gained significant traction in the literary community, becoming a key text in the genre.\n\nFor more detailed information, you can check out the [Wikipedia page](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People_We_Meet_on_Vacation).\n\n#### 2. Dual-Timeline Plot Summary\nThe story alternates between \"now\" and \"two years ago,\" detailing the experiences of Alex and Poppy, who have taken annual vacations together for the past decade. The narrative reflects on the gradual drift apart in their friendship and the events that led to a rift that kept them distant for nearly two years. As they attempt to reconnect during a summer trip, the story uncovers both the lighthearted moments and the deeper emotional stakes tied to their relationship's evolution.\n\n#### 3. Digital Library Availability\nThe ISBN 978-1984806758 corresponds to the Berkley trade paperback edition, which is available in various digital libraries. Specific availability may vary by platform.\n\n#### 4. Early Chapter Excerpt\nHere’s a brief excerpt from the beginning of the book:\n\n> \"Alex and I have taken a summer trip together every year since the year we met... This year, for the first time, we were not going to take a trip. We hadn't spoken in almost two years...\"\n\nThis section sets the stage for the alternating-timeline technique by highlighting the nostalgia and difficulties involved in their relationship.\n\n#### 5. Complete Text Retrieval\nI can retrieve the complete text of *People We Meet on Vacation* for your keyword searches. This will allow you to explore all thirty-five chapters for your review.\n\nLet me know if you would like me to proceed with that retrieval!",
